<XDFPATCH uniqueid="0x1000"><title>Disable PAIR valve</title><description>Normal and diagnostic air-induction commands. Enabled means firmware control is available, not that the valve is currently open. Apply = disabled; Remove = enabled. Use the whole patch, not individual entries. Correct the startup checksum after saving. Code-checked; hardware operation has not been validated.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="6"/><XDFPATCHENTRY name="Part 1" address="0x79EF" datasize="0x0003" patchdata="4DF001" basedata="4CF001"/><XDFPATCHENTRY name="Part 2" address="0x8C65" datasize="0x0003" patchdata="4DF001" basedata="4CF001"/></XDFPATCH>
<XDFPATCH uniqueid="0x1001"><title>Disable Immobilizer</title><description>Authentication configuration read by startup and runtime code. Detected from the bytes, including existing immobilizer-off BINs. Apply = disabled; Remove = enabled. Use the whole patch, not individual entries. Correct the startup checksum after saving. Code-checked; hardware operation has not been validated.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="6"/><XDFPATCHENTRY name="Part 1" address="0x2E19" datasize="0x0001" patchdata="80" basedata="00"/></XDFPATCH>
<XDFPATCH uniqueid="0x1002"><title>Disable Overrun cut</title><description>Disabling bypasses the overrun routine and restores its normal fuel multiplier. Sensor thresholds, shared throttle state and rev-limit cuts remain unchanged. Apply = disabled; Remove = enabled. Use the whole patch, not individual entries. Correct the startup checksum after saving. Code-checked; hardware operation has not been validated.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="6"/><XDFPATCHENTRY name="Part 1" address="0x1C51" datasize="0x0001" patchdata="7D" basedata="7D"/><XDFPATCHENTRY name="Part 2" address="0x1C56" datasize="0x0001" patchdata="85" basedata="85"/><XDFPATCHENTRY name="Part 3" address="0x566B" datasize="0x0003" patchdata="066F8F" basedata="F60914"/><XDFPATCHENTRY name="Part 4" address="0x57A2" datasize="0x0003" patchdata="066FB7" basedata="F60920"/></XDFPATCH>
<XDFPATCH uniqueid="0x1003"><title>Disable O2 sensor / feedback</title><description>Disabling stops O2 feedback and new faults 24, 31 and 32. Normal fuel maps remain selected. Existing stored faults are retained. Apply = disabled; Remove = enabled. Use the whole patch, not individual entries. Correct the startup checksum after saving. Code-checked; hardware operation has not been validated.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="6"/><XDFPATCHENTRY name="Part 1" address="0x1E8E" datasize="0x0001" patchdata="00" basedata="80"/><XDFPATCHENTRY name="Part 2" address="0x4C10" datasize="0x0003" patchdata="F6368E" basedata="F6368E"/><XDFPATCHENTRY name="Part 3" address="0x8000" datasize="0x0003" patchdata="F6368E" basedata="F6368E"/></XDFPATCH>
<XDFPATCH uniqueid="0x1004"><title>Disable Sidestand cut-off</title><description>Disabling allows the ECU to run with the stand down and suppresses new fault 19. The external starter-relay interlock still applies. Apply = disabled; Remove = enabled. Use the whole patch, not individual entries. Correct the startup checksum after saving. Code-checked; hardware operation has not been validated.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="6"/><XDFPATCHENTRY name="Part 1" address="0x2E08" datasize="0x0001" patchdata="80" basedata="00"/><XDFPATCHENTRY name="Part 2" address="0xAAC4" datasize="0x0004" patchdata="1D088C80" basedata="1C088C80"/></XDFPATCH>
<XDFPATCH uniqueid="0x1005"><title>Disable Lean-angle cut-off</title><description>Disabling removes ECU tip-over detection and the sensor fault-41 path: the engine may keep running after a fall. Existing latches or stored faults can still inhibit starting. Apply = disabled; Remove = enabled. Use the whole patch, not individual entries. Correct the startup checksum after saving. Code-checked; hardware operation has not been validated.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="6"/><XDFPATCHENTRY name="Part 1" address="0x2E2D" datasize="0x0001" patchdata="80" basedata="00"/></XDFPATCH>
<XDFPATCH uniqueid="0x1006"><title>CO full-range override</title><description>Keeps dashboard CO correction at full strength across the running range. Apply = override enabled; Remove = stock fade-out. Use the whole patch, not individual entries. Correct the startup checksum after saving. Code-checked; hardware operation has not been validated.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="6"/><XDFPATCHENTRY name="Part 1" address="0x1C78" datasize="0x0015" patchdata="14001C000080FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF" basedata="14001C000080FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF0000"/><XDFPATCHENTRY name="Part 2" address="0x5E8E" datasize="0x0015" patchdata="CE3478FC092016BBCF7A099EF60A00167A2B7A0964" basedata="CE3478FC092016BBCF7A099EF60A00167A2B7A0964"/><XDFPATCHENTRY name="Part 3" address="0x622B" datasize="0x002B" patchdata="C0802419CB8086801816F6099E12C30080180E8680181624118600200DB6099E12C300808B80240286FF3D" basedata="C0802419CB8086801816F6099E12C30080180E8680181624118600200DB6099E12C300808B80240286FF3D"/><XDFPATCHENTRY name="Part 4" address="0xB155" datasize="0x000A" patchdata="B60B117A0A001C089080" basedata="B60B117A0A001C089080"/></XDFPATCH>
<XDFPATCH uniqueid="0x1007"><title>Speedo disable</title><description>Apply one speed patch at a time; Remove it before selecting another. Zero remains zero; output is clamped to 0–255 pulses per reply. This changes dashboard speed and distance reporting only. Correct the startup checksum after saving. Code-checked; hardware operation has not been validated.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="6"/><XDFPATCHENTRY name="Part 1" address="0x4303" datasize="0x0006" patchdata="16B1007A08A9" basedata="B60B067A08A9"/><XDFPATCHENTRY name="Part 2" address="0x9900" datasize="0x0018" patchdata="398600383DFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF565353011400FFFF" basedata="FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF"/></XDFPATCH>
